    <with|font-size|1.6|font-series|bold|color|dark red|Renormalisation: why
    two of them>

    <vspace|0.3cm>

    <with|color|dark grey|Lecture 5>

    \;
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Scales and power counting>

    \;

    <\equation*>
      g<rsub|q>=\<gamma\>*q<rsup|-1/2><around|(|<text|dimensionless
      coupling>|)>,<space|2em>r<rsub|q>=<around|(|q/\<gamma\>|)><rsup|1/2>(\<gamma\>*r<rsub|q><rsup|2>=q:<text|nonlinearity>\<approx\><text|regulator>).
    </equation*>

    Free field at resolution <math|q>: <math|<math-up|Var>X<rsub|q><around|(|x|)>\<lesssim\>q<rsup|1/2>>,
    typical size <math|q<rsup|1/4>=g<rsub|q><rsup|1/2>*r<rsub|q>\<ll\>r<rsub|q>>.

    Rooted norm of a vertex <math|T<around|(|x<rsub|1>,\<ldots\>,x<rsub|k>|)>>
    and field ball:

    <\equation*>
      s<around|(|T|)>=max<rsub|i> sup<rsub|x<rsub|i>>
      <big|int><around|\||T|\|>*<big|prod><rsub|j\<ne\>i>\<mathd\>x<rsub|j>,<space|2em><math-ss|S><rsub|k><around|(|f|)>=sup<rsub|\<cal-B\><rsub|q>>
      s*<around|(|D<rsup|k>*f|)>,<space|2em>\<cal-B\><rsub|q>=<around|{|<around|\<\|\|\>|y|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<infty\>>\<less\>2*r<rsub|q>|}>.
    </equation*>

    Natural size of the <math|k>th vertex of the <strong|loop corrections>:

    <\equation*>
      <math-ss|S><rsub|k>\<lesssim\>g<rsub|q>*<space|0.17em>q*<space|0.17em>r<rsub|q><rsup|2-k>*<space|2em><around|(|k=4:\<gamma\>*g<rsub|q>|)>.
    </equation*>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The loop estimate>

    \;

    <\myframed>
      <strong|Loop estimate>

      A closed loop with <math|p> vertices:
      <math|s<around|(|<text|loop>|)>\<le\>C*a<rsub|2><around|(|q|)>*<space|0.17em>q<rsup|-<around|(|p-1|)>>*<big|prod><rsub|i>s<around|(|T<rsub|i>|)>>
      (two propagators in <math|L<rsup|2>>, the others in operator norm).
      After the <math|q> integration a one-loop term is of size
      <math|g<rsub|q>*q*r<rsub|q><rsup|2-k>>; every further loop gains a
      factor <math|g<rsub|q>>.
    </myframed>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The seed and the corrections>

    \;

    <with|font-series|bold|Seed> (one loop, Lecture 4, Ex. 8.7(b)): replace
    <math|D<rsup|2>*\<Gamma\>> by <math|D<rsup|2>*U=\<gamma\>*y<rsup|2>> and
    integrate from <math|q=\<infty\>>,

    <\equation*>
      \<cal-L\><rsub|q><around|(|y|)>=<tfrac|1|2><math-up|Tr><around*|[|log
      <around|(|I+C<rsub|q><rsup|1/2>*\<gamma\>*y<rsup|2>*C<rsub|q><rsup|1/2>|)>-C<rsub|q><rsup|1/2>*\<gamma\>*y<rsup|2>*C<rsub|q><rsup|1/2>|]>=<big|sum><rsub|j\<ge\>2><frac|<around|(|-1|)><rsup|j+1>|2*j><math-up|Tr><around|(|C<rsub|q>*\<gamma\>*y<rsup|2>|)><rsup|j>.
    </equation*>

    Quartic term <math|=> bubble, <math|s*<around|(|D<rsup|4>*\<cal-L\><rsub|q><around|(|0|)>|)>=6*\<gamma\><rsup|2>*a<rsub|2><around|(|q|)>>.

    <with|font-series|bold|Corrections.> <math|\<Pi\>> removes the constant
    and quadratic jets, <math|M<rsub|q>=\<mu\><rsub|q>+\<Theta\><rsub|q>> a
    quadratic path,

    <\equation*>
      <with|math-font|cal*|T><rsub|q><around|[|M,h|]>=<tfrac|1|2><math-up|Tr><around*|[|<around|(|K<rsub|q>+M<rsub|q>+D<rsup|2>*<around|(|U+h|)>|)><rsup|-1>-<around|(|K<rsub|q>+M<rsub|q>|)><rsup|-1>|]>,
    </equation*>

    <\equation*>
      h<rsup|<around|[|0|]>>=\<cal-L\>,<space|2em>h<rsup|<around|[|j+1|]>><rsub|q>=\<cal-L\><rsub|q>-<big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>>\<Pi\>*<around*|(|<with|math-font|cal*|T><rsub|s><around|[|M,h<rsup|<around|[|j|]>>|]>-\<partial\><rsub|s>*\<cal-L\><rsub|s>|)>\<mathd\>s,<space|1em>j=0,1,
    </equation*>

    <\equation*>
      \<Gamma\><rsup|<math-up|o>><rsub|q>=U+<tfrac|1|2><around|\<langle\>|y,M<rsub|q>*y|\<rangle\>>+h<rsup|<around|[|2|]>><rsub|q><space|1em><text|on
      the ball>.
    </equation*>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The mass>

    \;

    The quadratic jet is not iterated: it is solved exactly by <math|M>,

    <\equation*>
      \<partial\><rsub|q>*M<rsub|q>=-\<gamma\><math-up|Tr><around|(|R<rsub|0,q><rsup|2>|)>*<space|0.17em>I-<tfrac|1|2><math-up|Ctr><rsub|R<rsub|0,q><rsup|2>>D<rsup|4>*h<rsup|<around|[|2|]>><rsub|q><around|(|0|)>,<space|2em>R<rsub|0,q>=<around|(|K<rsub|q>+M<rsub|q>|)><rsup|-1>,
    </equation*>

    with <strong|mixed boundary conditions> <math|\<mu\><rsub|q<rsub|0>>=0>
    (physical mass) and <math|\<Theta\><rsub|q>\<to\>0> as
    <math|q\<to\>\<infty\>> (first moment). Bare mass
    <math|\<mu\><rsub|N>=lim<rsub|q\<to\>\<infty\>> \<mu\><rsub|q>>: an
    <strong|output> of the flow.

    <\proposition*>
      <dueto|for <math|q<rsub|0>> large, uniformly in <math|N>>Unique
      solution in a ball, with <math|<around|\||\<mu\><rsub|q>|\|>\<le\>C*\<gamma\>*<sqrt|q>>,
      <math|v<rsub|1><around|(|\<Theta\><rsub|q>|)>\<le\>C*\<gamma\><rsup|2>*q<rsup|-1/2>>;
      increments <math|\<cal-N\><rsub|k>*<around|(|h<rsup|<around|[|j|]>>-h<rsup|<around|[|j-1|]>>|)>\<le\>C<rsub|k>*g<rsub|q><rsup|j+1>*q*r<rsub|q><rsup|2-k>>,
      <math|4\<le\>k\<le\>10-2*j>, <math|j=1,2>; and the defect of
      <math|\<Gamma\><rsup|<math-up|o>>>

      <\equation*>
        <math-ss|S><rsub|4><around|(|e<rsup|<math-up|o>><rsub|q>|)>\<le\>C*\<gamma\><rsup|5>*q<rsup|-3>.
      </equation*>
    </proposition*>

    Ideas: trace Lipschitz estimate by loops; integrability at
    <math|q=\<infty\>> for <math|k\<ge\>4>; contraction for <math|M>;
    derivative budget <math|10\<to\>8\<to\>6>.
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Two mass renormalisations>

    \;

    The two divergent self-energies of Lecture 4 Ÿ10.2:

    <\itemize>
      <item><strong|Tadpole>: <math|-\<gamma\>*<big|int><rsub|q<rsub|0>><rsup|\<infty\>><math-up|Tr>R<rsub|0,q><rsup|2><space|0.17em>\<mathd\>q\<approx\>-3*\<lambda\><math-up|Tr>C\<sim\>-N>.
      Wick ordering: <math|<frac|\<lambda\>|4>*\<varphi\><rsup|4>-<frac|3|2>*\<lambda\>*c*\<varphi\><rsup|2>=<frac|\<lambda\>|4>*H<rsub|4>*<around|(|\<varphi\>;c|)>+>const.

      <item><strong|Sunset>: contracting the bubble in
      <math|D<rsup|4>*h<around|(|0|)>> with <math|R<rsub|0><rsup|2>> and
      integrating gives the two-loop self-energy,

      <\equation*>
        6*\<lambda\><rsup|2>*<big|int>C<rsup|3>\<approx\><frac|3*\<lambda\><rsup|2>|8*\<pi\><rsup|2>>*log
        N<space|1em>(=2*\<gamma\><rsub|T>*<text|of Lecture 4, with
        >\<lambda\><rsub|<with|math-font-family|rm|L3>>=\<lambda\>/4).
      </equation*>
    </itemize>

    Power counting: nothing else. In the flow: the integrals from
    <math|q=\<infty\>> of all vertices with <math|k\<ge\>4> legs converge;
    only the quadratic jet needs a boundary condition.

    <math|\<mu\><rsub|q>> at fixed <math|q> has a limit as
    <math|N\<to\>\<infty\>>; <math|\<mu\><rsub|N>> does not. <strong|Never
    interchange the two limits.>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Two correction steps>

    \;

    Backward propagator <math|\<approx\>s/q>, so
    <math|Z<rsub|q>\<approx\><big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>><frac|s|q>*b<rsub|s>\<mathd\>s>,
    and on the ball <math|<around|\||b<rsub|s>|\|>\<lesssim\>s<rsup|-1><math-ss|S><rsub|4><around|(|e<rsub|s>|)>*r<rsub|s><rsup|3>>.
    After <math|n> steps, <math|<math-ss|S><rsub|4><around|(|e<rsub|s>|)>\<lesssim\>g<rsub|s><rsup|n+1>*s<rsup|1/2>*r<rsub|s><rsup|-4>>:

    <tabular*|<tformat|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-valign|c>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-tborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|4|4|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<table|<row|<cell|steps
    <math|n>>|<cell|<math|<math-ss|S><rsub|4><around|(|e<rsub|s>|)>>>|<cell|<math|<around|\||b<rsub|s>|\|>>>|<cell|<math|<big|int><rsub|q><rsup|\<infty\>><frac|s|q><around|\||b<rsub|s>|\|>\<mathd\>s>>>|<row|<cell|<math|0>>|<cell|<math|\<gamma\><rsup|3>*s<rsup|-2>>>|<cell|<math|\<gamma\><rsup|3/2>*s<rsup|-3/2>>>|<cell|<math|\<infty\>>
    (power)>>|<row|<cell|<math|1>>|<cell|<math|\<gamma\><rsup|4>*s<rsup|-5/2>>>|<cell|<math|\<gamma\><rsup|5/2>*s<rsup|-2>>>|<cell|<math|\<infty\>>
    (log)>>|<row|<cell|<math|2>>|<cell|<math|\<gamma\><rsup|5>*s<rsup|-3>>>|<cell|<math|\<gamma\><rsup|7/2>*s<rsup|-5/2>>>|<cell|<math|2*\<gamma\><rsup|7/2>*q<rsup|-3/2>>>>>>>

    <strong|Two steps are the minimum, and suffice.> The defect of one step
    is borderline in the backward equation, as the sunset is borderline in
    the mass. (Heuristic threshold for <math|\<Phi\><rsup|4><rsub|3>>:
    <math|n\<gtr\>1>; the general theory's sufficient criterion is
    <math|<around|(|n+2|)>*\<varkappa\>\<gtr\><around|(|3+\<varkappa\>|)>/2>,
    <math|\<varkappa\>=<frac|1|2>>, met by <math|n=2>.)
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <vspace*|2.5cm>

    \;

    <with|font-size|1.6|font-series|bold|color|dark red|The flow at large
    fields>

    <vspace|0.3cm>

    <with|color|dark grey|Lecture 5>

    \;
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The large-field problem>

    \;

    All bounds hold on <math|\<cal-B\><rsub|q>=<around|{|<around|\<\|\|\>|y|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<infty\>>\<less\>2*r<rsub|q>|}>>
    only. The free field exceeds <math|r<rsub|q>> with small, nonzero
    probability, and nothing a priori controls the interacting forecast. We
    need <math|<wide|\<Gamma\>|\<bar\>><rsub|q>> <strong|defined and
    uniformly convex for all fields>.

    <\myframed>
      <strong|Scalar model>

      <math|\<cal-L\><rsub|q><around|(|y|)>=<frac|1|2>*<around|[|log
      <around|(|1+\<gamma\>*y<rsup|2>/q|)>-\<gamma\>*y<rsup|2>/q|]>>: power
      series of radius exactly <math|r<rsub|q>> (singularities at
      <math|\<pm\>\<mathi\>r<rsub|q>>). Truncations at even <math|j\<ge\>4>
      are unbounded below. The exact function is harmless,
      <math|<around|\||\<cal-L\><rsub|q><rprime|''>|\|>\<le\><frac|9|8>*\<gamma\>/q>.
    </myframed>

    Perturbative control for <math|<around|\||y|\|>\<lesssim\>r<rsub|q>>;
    outside, a non-perturbative replacement that keeps the structure the
    estimates use: <strong|coercivity>, carried by the bare quartic.

    One site: <math|q*y+\<lambda\>*y<rsup|3>=p>, noise coefficient
    <math|H<rsub|q><around|(|y|)>=<around|(|q+\<gamma\>*y<rsup|2>|)><rsup|-1>\<le\>q<rsup|-1>\<wedge\><around|(|\<gamma\>*y<rsup|2>|)><rsup|-1>>.
    Large fields are <strong|more elliptic and less noisy>.
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|Clipping>

    \;

    <math|\<tau\>> smooth odd, <math|\<tau\><around|(|u|)>=u> on
    <math|<around|[|-1,1|]>>, constant outside <math|<around|[|-2,2|]>>,
    <math|0\<le\>\<tau\><rprime|'>\<le\>1>;

    <\equation*>
      \<kappa\><rsub|q><around|(|y|)>=r<rsub|q>*\<tau\>*<around|(|y/r<rsub|q>|)>,<space|2em><wide|\<Gamma\>|\<bar\>><rsub|q>=U+<tfrac|1|2><around|\<langle\>|y,M<rsub|q>*y|\<rangle\>>+<wide|h|~><rsub|q>,<space|2em><wide|h|~><rsub|q>=h<rsup|<around|[|2|]>><rsub|q>\<circ\>\<kappa\><rsub|q>.
    </equation*>

    The quartic and quadratic parts are <strong|not> clipped. Globally:
    <math|s*<around|(|D<rsup|j>*<wide|h|~><rsub|q>|)>\<le\>C*g<rsub|q>*q*r<rsub|q><rsup|2-j>>
    (<math|j=2,3,4>), <math|s*<around|(|D<rsup|2>*\<partial\><rsub|q>*<wide|h|~><rsub|q>|)>\<le\>C*g<rsub|q>>.

    <\myframed>
      <strong|Global coercivity>

      For all <math|y>: <math|c*<around|(|K<rsub|q>+\<gamma\>*y<rsup|2>|)>\<le\>H<rsub|q><around|(|y|)><rsup|-1>\<le\>C*<around|(|K<rsub|q>+\<gamma\>*y<rsup|2>|)>>,

      <\equation*>
        <around|\<\|\|\>|H<rsub|q><around|(|y|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|p\<to\>p>\<le\><frac|1+C*<around|(|g<rsub|q>+g<rsub|q><rsup|2>|)>|q>,<space|2em><math-up|diag>H<rsub|q><around|(|y|)><rsup|2>\<le\>C*a<rsub|2><around|(|q|)>.
      </equation*>
    </myframed>

    Neumann series for <math|H=<around|(|I+G*<around|(|M+D<rsup|2>*<wide|h|~>|)>|)><rsup|-1>*G>,
    <math|G=<around|(|K<rsub|q>+\<gamma\>*y<rsup|2>|)><rsup|-1>\<le\>C<rsub|q>>.
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The complete defect>

    \;

    <math|b=b<rsup|<math-up|b>>+b<rsup|<math-up|l>>>,
    <math|b<rsup|<math-up|b>>=-H*<space|0.17em>D*\<kappa\>*<space|0.17em>D*e<rsup|<math-up|o>>*<around|(|\<kappa\>*y|)>>,
    <math|t<rsub|q><around|(|y|)>=y*<with|math-font|Bbb|1><rsub|<around|\||y|\|>\<gtr\>r<rsub|q>>>.

    <\proposition*>
      <dueto|uniformly in <math|y>, <math|N>, <math|p>>

      <\equation*>
        <around|\<\|\|\>|b<rsup|<math-up|b>><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|p>\<le\>C*\<gamma\><rsup|7/2>*q<rsup|-5/2>,<space|2em><around|\<\|\|\>|b<rsup|<math-up|l>><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|p>\<le\>C*\<gamma\>*q<rsup|-3/2><around*|(|<around|\<\|\|\>|t<rsub|q>*<around|\<\|\|\>|<rsub|p>+r<rsub|q><rsup|-1>|\<\|\|\>>*y<rsup|2>*<with|math-font|Bbb|1><rsub|<around|\||y|\|>\<gtr\>r<rsub|q>>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|p>|)>,
      </equation*>

      <\equation*>
        <around|\<\|\|\>|b<rsup|<math-up|l>><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|2><rsup|2>\<le\>C*\<gamma\><rsup|4>*q<rsup|-5><around|\<\|\|\>|t<rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|6><rsup|6>.
      </equation*>
    </proposition*>

    Sources of <math|b<rsup|<math-up|l>>> (four groups): the mass term
    <math|M<rprime|'>*y-J*M<rprime|'>*\<kappa\>*y> (<math|J=D*\<kappa\>>,
    <math|M<rprime|'>=\<partial\><rsub|q>*M>; quadratic part unclipped, flow
    computed at <math|\<kappa\>*y>); the motion of the clip; quartic vertex
    at <math|y> vs correction at <math|\<kappa\>*y>; chain-rule terms with
    <math|\<kappa\><rprime|''>,\<kappa\><rprime|'''>>. All vanish if
    <math|<around|\<\|\|\>|y|\<\|\|\>><rsub|\<infty\>>\<le\>r<rsub|q>>.

    <\myframed>
      <strong|The point>

      <math|b<rsup|<math-up|l>>> is as large as the whole drift, but
      <strong|supported on large fields>. It is controlled by how often the
      actual dynamics visits them: <math|<big|int>q<rsup|-3/2>*\<gamma\><around|\<\|\|\>|t<rsub|q><around|(|Y<rsub|q>|)>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|6><rsup|6><space|0.17em>\<mathd\>q>
      (Lecture 6).
    </myframed>
  </hidden>|<\hidden>
    <mytitle|The coordinate equation>

    \;

    With <math|D*U=<frac|\<gamma\>|3>*y<rsup|3>>:

    <\equation*>
      K<rsub|q>*\<Phi\><rsub|q>=K<rsub|q>*<around*|(|Y<rsub|q>+\<varrho\><rsub|q><around|(|Y<rsub|q>|)>|)>+<frac|\<gamma\>|3>*Y<rsub|q><rsup|3>,<space|2em>\<varrho\><rsub|q><around|(|y|)>=C<rsub|q>*<around*|(|M<rsub|q>*y+D*<wide|h|~><rsub|q><around|(|y|)>|)>,<space|1em><around|\<\|\|\>|D*\<varrho\><rsub|q>|\<\|\|\>><rsub|p\<to\>p>\<le\>C*<around|(|g<rsub|q>+g<rsub|q><rsup|2>|)>.
    </equation*>

    <strong|Up to a small Lipschitz perturbation, the forecast solves the
    cubic elliptic equation> <math|K<rsub|q>*<around|(|Y+\<varrho\>|)>+<frac|\<gamma\>|3>*Y<rsup|3>=K<rsub|q>*\<Phi\><rsub|q>>
    driven by the field at resolution <math|q>.

    <with|font-series|bold|Summary of today>, at every lattice:

    <\itemize>
      <item><math|\<mu\><rsub|N>>, <math|M<rsub|q>> and a globally convex
      <math|<wide|\<Gamma\>|\<bar\>><rsub|q>>, all deterministic;

      <item>the exact FBSDE for <math|<around|(|Y,Z|)>>;

      <item>a source whose bounded-field part is integrable (two steps), and
      whose large-field part is controlled by sixth powers of <math|Y> on
      large fields.
    </itemize>

    <with|font-series|bold|Next:> estimates on <math|<around|(|Y,Z|)>>
    uniform in <math|N>.
  </hidden>>
